Every clinician should work with a patient for a prolonged-opioid-use-prevention.
Every clinician should prescribe an as-needed-opioid instead-of a scheduled-opioid and should advise an as-needed-opioid instead-of a scheduled-opioid.
An as-needed-opioid-example contains 5 hydrocodone-milligrams and contains 325 acetaminophen-milligrams and uses 1 tablet at an interval of at least 4 hours for a moderate-to-severe-pain.
A scheduled-opioid-example uses 1 tablet at an interval of 4 hours.
If a patient has a prolonged-around-the-clock-opioid-use for a few-day-period then every clinician should encourage an opioid-taper and should include an opioid-taper.
